                "meta_id": "meta:037bef2d48ae",
                "text": "[Concepts: type, cid, types, term, can] 3.6 Notes 43 called big-step semantics (or sometimes natural semantics), directly formu- lates the notion of “this term evaluates to that ﬁnal value,” written t ⇓ v. The big-step evaluation rules for our language of boolean and arithmetic expres- sions look like this: v ⇓ v t1 ⇓ true t2 ⇓ v2 if t1 then t2 else t3 ⇓ v2 t1 ⇓ false t3 ⇓ v3 if t1 then t2 else t3",
